      "date": "1977-08-03",
      "kind": "permit appeal",
      "description": "The Board of Permit Appeals overruled the Department of Public Works' denial of a permit to erect a sign at 712 Geary Street, with stipulations that the sign conform to Planning Code standards, the hanging portion at the bottom of the sign be removed, and the sign be painted with a clear fire retardant paint, with a certificate attesting to the fire retardant properties of the paint attached to the Board's Decision and Order.",
